Synchronizing Kubernetes Applications
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Understand the difference between automatic and manual synchronization in Argo CD
Configure auto-sync policies for GitOps applications
Perform manual synchronization of applications when needed
Test and verify synchronization between Git repositories and Kubernetes clusters
Troubleshoot common synchronization issues in GitOps workflows
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Kubernetes concepts (pods, services, deployments)
Familiarity with Git version control system
Knowledge of YAML file structure and syntax
Understanding of GitOps principles and workflows
Completed previous labs on Kubernetes and Argo CD basics
