Subtask 3.2: Test Sync Policies and Options
Step 1: Create an application with specific sync policies

mkdir -p apps/redis-app
cat << EOF > apps/redis-app/deployment.yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: redis-deployment
  namespace: default
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: redis
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: redis
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: redis
        image: redis:6.2
        ports:
        - containerPort: 6379
EOF

git add apps/redis-app/
git commit -m "Add redis application"
Step 2: Create application with advanced sync policies

cat << EOF > redis-app.yaml
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: redis-app
  namespace: argocd
spec:
  project: default
  source:
    repoURL: file:///home/$(whoami)/gitops-demo
    targetRevision: HEAD
    path: apps/redis-app
  destination:
    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
    namespace: default
  syncPolicy:
    automated:
      prune: true
      selfHeal: true
    retry:
      limit: 5
      backoff:
        duration: 5s
        factor: 2
        maxDuration: 3m
    syncOptions:
    - CreateNamespace=true
    - PrunePropagationPolicy=foreground
    - PruneLast=true
EOF

kubectl apply -f redis-app.yaml
Subtask 3.3: Test Conflict Resolution
Step 1: Create a manual change in Kubernetes

# Scale the nginx deployment manually (outside of Git)
kubectl scale deployment nginx-deployment --replicas=5
kubectl get pods -l app=nginx
Step 2: Observe self-healing behavior

# Watch how auto-sync corrects the drift
watch -n 3 "kubectl get pods -l app=nginx | wc -l"
Step 3: Test prune functionality

# Add a temporary resource
cat << EOF > apps/nginx-app/configmap.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: nginx-config
  namespace: default
data:
  nginx.conf: |
    server {
        listen 80;
        location / {
            return 200 'Hello from Nginx!';
        }
    }
EOF

git add apps/nginx-app/configmap.yaml
git commit -m "Add nginx configmap"

# Wait for sync, then remove the file
sleep 30
rm apps/nginx-app/configmap.yaml
git add apps/nginx-app/configmap.yaml
git commit -m "Remove nginx configmap"

# Verify the configmap is pruned
kubectl get configmap nginx-config || echo "ConfigMap successfully pruned"
Subtask 3.4: Monitor and Troubleshoot Synchronization
Step 1: Check application health and sync status

# Get detailed application information
argocd app get nginx-app --show-params
argocd app get apache-app --show-params
argocd app get redis-app --show-params
Step 2: View synchronization history

# Check sync history for applications
argocd app history nginx-app
argocd app history apache-app
Step 3: Test sync with different strategies

# Force sync with replace strategy
argocd app sync nginx-app --strategy=force

# Sync only specific resources
argocd app sync apache-app --resource=apps:Deployment:apache-deployment
Step 4: Demonstrate rollback functionality

# Get current revision
CURRENT_REVISION=$(argocd app get nginx-app -o json | jq -r '.status.sync.revision')
echo "Current revision: $CURRENT_REVISION"

# Make a change
sed -i 's/replicas: 2/replicas: 4/' apps/nginx-app/deployment.yaml
git add apps/nginx-app/deployment.yaml
git commit -m "Scale nginx to 4 replicas"

# Wait for sync, then rollback
sleep 30
argocd app rollback nginx-app $CURRENT_REVISION

# Verify rollback
kubectl get deployment nginx-deployment -o jsonpath='{.spec.replicas}'
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Application Stuck in Progressing State
Symptoms: Application shows "Progressing" status for extended periods

Solution:

# Check application events
argocd app get <app-name> --show-operation

# Check Kubernetes events
kubectl get events --sort-by=.metadata.creationTimestamp

# Force refresh
argocd app get <app-name> --refresh
Issue 2: Auto-Sync Not Working
Symptoms: Changes in Git are not automatically applied

Solution:

# Verify sync policy configuration
argocd app get <app-name> -o yaml | grep -A 10 syncPolicy

# Check if application is healthy
argocd app get <app-name> | grep Health

# Manual refresh to trigger sync
argocd app sync <app-name>
Issue 3: Resource Conflicts
Symptoms: Sync fails due to resource conflicts

Solution:

# Use force sync to override conflicts
argocd app sync <app-name> --force

# Check resource differences
argocd app diff <app-name>

# Use replace strategy for stubborn resources
argocd app sync <app-name> --strategy=force
